A busy spin of ~15ms per frame means about 90% of 6 minutes total is CPU spin. Atomics.wait on a SharedArrayBuffer is a better spin — it blocks the thread efficiently without burning CPU. Node supports Atomics.wait. That's the clean approach:

```ts
const spinBuf = new SharedArrayBuffer(4);
const spin = (ms: number) => {
  const end = Date.now() + ms;
  while (true) {
    const left = end - Date.now();
    if (left <= 0) return;
    Atomics.wait(new Int32Array(spinBuf, 0), 0, 0, Math.min(left, 100));
  }
};
```

